// One half of a same-named private helper, kept in its own module.
//
// `reading` has no `///` block and nothing asks for it by name, so this module
// is the only thing that can mean it. Inlining puts both halves into one
// translation unit, and before they were kept apart the checker typed this
// file's call against beta's signature and reported the mismatch here, in a
// file whose author had not touched beta at all.

/// One more than the length of `s`.
alpha_reading(s: str) -> int => reading(s) + 1

reading(s: str) -> int => s.length()
